          deepDive: "**〜たら／〜ば それまでだ** says *if ~ happens, that's the end of it — all the effort, hardship and money spent so far is wasted* (the usage note: 今までの努力や苦労や費用が全て無駄になる). それまで = *up to that point*: the condition marks where everything stops.\n\nConnection: **V-たら** or **V-ば + それまでだ**; the negative 〜なければそれまでだ is common (使いこなせる技術者がいなければそれまでだ *without technicians who can operate it, it's useless*). Usually the first half mentions something valuable or an effort (有名企業に就職しても, 新型の医療機器をそろえても, 頑張るのもいいが) and the condition is what would make it worthless.\n\nTypical uses:\n- A warning: all your preparation is for nothing if X happens (無理して病気になったらそれまでだ *if you overdo it and get sick, it's all over*). The 部長 in the sample: 先を越されたらそれまでだぞ *if a rival beats us to it, that's the end*.\n- A sober observation about fragility: 携帯電話は便利だが、バッテリーが切れればそれまでだ.\n- Encouragement framed negatively: あきらめたらそれまでだ (*if you give up, it's over — so don't*).\n\nRegister: neutral; used in speech (often with ぞ / よ) and in writing.\n\nCompare:\n- **〜たら／〜ば終わりだ**: nearly the same meaning, more colloquial. それまでだ sounds a little more philosophical.\n- **〜たが最後** (#33): *once ~ happens, (an unwanted state) inevitably follows*: 彼に話したが最後、会社中に広まる. たが最後 predicts a bad consequence; それまでだ says everything stops and is wasted.\n- **〜までだ / 〜までのことだ** (#82): *(if so,) I'll simply ~* — attaches to the **dictionary form** and announces a calm fallback action: だめなら次の会社を受けるまでのことだ. それまでだ attaches to a **conditional** and says that nothing more can be done.\n- **Vたまでのことだ** (#93): *I merely did ~* — downplays one's own past action.\n\nPitfall: それまでだ is not *until then*: ✗バッテリーが切れればそれまでだ ≠ バッテリーが切れるまで使おう (option b in the practice). It is also not a judgment that the thing is useless in general (option c: バッテリーが切れるから無駄だ) — the point is that it becomes useless **once** the condition happens.\n\nJLPT tip: in paraphrase questions, それまでだ ≈ 〜たら使えない / 出られない / 何にもならない (the practice answers: バッテリーが切れたら使えない, 2回戦には出られない). In the Check, 使い方を知らなければ（それまでだ）: a fire extinguisher is worthless if you can't use it.",
